4123|         /* This verifies 'check', the absolute value of the actual stride
4124|          * passed in and detects overflow in the application calculation (i.e.
4125|          * if the app did actually pass in a non-zero 'row_stride'.
4126|          */
4127|         if (image->opaque != NULL && buffer != NULL && check >= png_row_stride)
4128|         {
4129|            /* Now check for overflow of the image buffer calculation; this
4130|             * limits the whole image size to 32 bits for API compatibility with
4131|             * the current, 32-bit, PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE macro.
4132|             *
4133|             * The PNG_IMAGE_BUFFER_SIZE macro is:
4134|             *
4135|             *    (PNG_IMAGE_PIXEL_COMPONENT_SIZE(fmt)*height*(row_stride))
4136|             *
4137|             * And the component size is always 1 or 2, so make sure that the
4138|             * number of *bytes* that the application is saying are available
4139|             * does actually fit into a 32-bit number.
